bevy_time::timer::Timer::from_seconds.documentation:
A timer which runs for `secs` seconds, in `mode`. Errors if `secs` is negative or not finite.

```multi-lang-example,lua
local Timer = import_namespace("time").Timer
local TimerMode = import_namespace("time").TimerMode
local timer = Timer.from_seconds(2, TimerMode.Repeating)
timer:tick(1)
assert(not timer:finished())
timer:tick(1.5)
assert(timer:finished())
```

```multi-lang-example,rhai
let Timer = import_namespace.call("time").Timer;
let TimerMode = import_namespace.call("time").TimerMode;
let timer = Timer.from_seconds.call(2.0, TimerMode.Repeating);
timer.tick.call(1.0);
assert(!timer.finished.call());
timer.tick.call(1.5);
assert(timer.finished.call());
```

bevy_ui::geometry::Val::px.documentation:
A length in logical pixels, such as `Val.px(100)` for 100 pixels.

```multi-lang-example,lua
local Node = import_namespace("ui").Node
local Val = import_namespace("ui").Val
local node = Node.new({ width = Val.px(100) })
assert(node.width[1] == 100)
```

```multi-lang-example,rhai
let Node = import_namespace.call("ui").Node;
let Val = import_namespace.call("ui").Val;
let node = Node.new_.call(#{ width: Val.px.call(100.0) });
assert(node.width[0] == 100.0);
```
